QingLuan Digital Signature Scheme - Implementations
===================================================

QingLuan (青鸾) is a post-quantum DIGITAL SIGNATURE scheme built on R-SDP
(Restricted Syndrome Decoding) + MPC-in-the-Head + Fiat-Shamir, instantiated
entirely with SM3 (GB/T 32905) and the SM3 Hash-DRBG (GM/T 0005). It contains
no RSA / ECC / DH / lattice component.


Overview
--------

Per algorithm-requirements item (6), this `Implementations/` directory contains
ONLY the three implementation categories and this README:

1. Reference_Implementation - four self-contained AlgorithmInstance folders
   (QingLuan-128 / -256 / -384 / -512), ISO C11, platform-independent. Each
   instance also carries its own API_PKC KAT generator under `api_pkc/`.
2. Optimized_Implementation  - reserved (Part 2 scope); placeholder README.txt only.
3. Additional_Implementation - reserved; placeholder README.txt only.
4. README (this file) - directory listing + brief description of each file.

Supporting material lives at the SUBMISSION ROOT (sibling of Implementations/),
outside this directory so the layout stays compliant with item (6):
- ../Test_Vectors/             - official KAT vectors (framework format).
- ../Supporting_Documentation/ - protocol_reference.md, parameters.md,
                                 security-argument.md, rsdp_estimator.py.
- ../Qingluan Algorithm Text.pdf, ../算法基本信息样例.pdf, ../知识产权声明.pdf.


Directory Structure
-------------------

Per item (6), each AlgorithmInstance is a single self-contained folder named
[AlgorithmInstance]. The security level is FIXED in that folder's
include/params.h, so the reference build needs NO compile-time -D flag.

\Implementations
  \Reference_Implementation
    \QingLuan-128                One instance, classical 128 / quantum 64 (NIST cat-1).
      \include
        api.h                    Public signature API (crypto_sign_*)
        params.h                 Parameters FIXED to this instance's level
        hash.h                   SM3-based hash/XOF interface (multi-pipe)
        fq_arith.h               F_p arithmetic (p = 127) declarations
        restr.h                  Restricted-set E = <2> mod 127 operations
        rsdp.h                   R-SDP matrix/error/syndrome operations
        mpc.h                    MPC-in-the-Head (CROSS-RSDP) operations
        sign.h                   Internal signature structures
        selftest.h               Self-test interface
        utils.h                  RNG, constant-time helpers, secure_zero
      \src
        fq_arith.c               Constant-time field arithmetic (Barrett)
        restr.c                  Constant-time restricted-set arithmetic
        hash.c                   SM3 + multi-pipe hash + XOF counter mode
        utils.c                  System entropy + SM3 Hash-DRBG + CT utilities
        rsdp.c                   Matrix expansion, error gen, syndrome packing
        mpc.c                    MPC-in-the-Head core (witness genuinely shared)
        keygen.c                 Key generation
        sign.c                   Signature generation
        verify.c                 Signature verification (checks R-SDP relation)
        selftest.c               Known-answer and flow self-tests
      \test
        main.c                   End-to-end round-trip + tamper-rejection test
        kat_gen.c                Internal determinism KAT (10 self-verified)
        test_{restr,rsdp,hash,mpc,sign}.c   Unit tests
        test_forgery.c           Public-key forgery regression gate
        test_determinism.c       Determinism + pinned-KAT regression
      \api_pkc                   OFFICIAL KAT generator (API_PKC framework).
        SIG_AlgorithmInstance.c/.h   QingLuan -> API_PKC SIG adapter
        hash_adapter.c           Multi-pipe SM3 / SM3-counter XOF on the
                                 framework sm3hash (byte-identical to ../src/hash.c)
        utils_adapter.c          Adapter RNG/utility layer (framework DRNG)
        hash.h                   Adapter-private hash/XOF struct layouts
        KAT_SIG.c                Framework KAT driver (unmodified)
        drng.c/.h, auxfunc.c/.h  Framework support files (unmodified)
        Makefile                 Level-fixed build; pulls ../src + ../include
      Makefile                   Self-contained reference build (no -D; -lbcrypt on Win)
      README.txt                 Per-instance notes
    \QingLuan-256                Same layout, classical 256 / quantum >= 128.
    \QingLuan-384                Same layout, classical 384 / quantum >= 192.
    \QingLuan-512                Same layout, classical 512 / quantum >= 256.

  \Optimized_Implementation      Reserved (Part 2 scope); placeholder README.txt.
  \Additional_Implementation     Reserved; placeholder README.txt.

  \README                        This file.


Security Levels and Sizes
-------------------------

Binding security = min(key-recovery, forgery), at or above each level's
classical target. Quantum is the conservative classical/2 full-Grover bound;
256/384/512 meet their quantum floors (128/192/256) with no credit. The 128
entry level is the exception: its raw quantum binding is 64-bit (= 128/2); the
"80-bit" entry floor is met as a NIST category-1 designation (AES-128 under
bounded-depth Grover), NOT as a literal 2^80 -- see
Supporting_Documentation/parameters.md section 4.1 note (1).
- QingLuan-128: classical 128-bit, quantum 64-bit (meets NIST cat-1 "80" floor)
- QingLuan-256: classical 256-bit, quantum >= 128-bit
- QingLuan-384: classical 384-bit, quantum >= 192-bit
- QingLuan-512: classical 512-bit, quantum >= 256-bit

Sizes (verified against compiled test/main.c; see Supporting_Documentation/
parameters.md section 7):
  Level         |pk|     |sk|     |sig|
  QingLuan-128    77 B    32 B    18 720 B
  QingLuan-256   153 B    64 B    74 248 B
  QingLuan-384   227 B    96 B   164 940 B
  QingLuan-512   302 B   128 B   292 816 B

MPC-in-the-Head signatures are inherently large; further compression
(seed tree / Merkle) and multi-platform tuning are Part 2 scope.


Symmetric Primitives (pure SM3)
-------------------------------

- Hash/commitment/Fiat-Shamir: multi-pipe SM3 with domain-separated pipe
  prefixes, output widened to 2*lambda bits (256/512/768/1024).
  Honest claim: this widening provides preimage / second-preimage / TCR up to
  the full width; it does NOT claim plain collision resistance above ~2^128
  (Joux multicollision). Every collision-relying use is salted (eTCR). See
  Supporting_Documentation/security-argument.md section 3.
- XOF: absorb with the multi-pipe hash, squeeze via SM3(input || counter).
- Randomness: SM3 Hash-DRBG (GM/T 0005). A 48/64-byte seed may be injected for
  deterministic KAT reproducibility without reducing entropy.


Build and Run (one Reference instance)
--------------------------------------

Each folder is self-contained and needs no -D flag. Example for QingLuan-128
(replace 128 with 256/384/512 for other levels):

  cd Reference_Implementation/QingLuan-128
  make                     # builds qingluan_test and qingluan_kat

Or directly with GCC (MinGW-w64; -lbcrypt only on Windows):
  gcc -Wall -Wextra -std=c11 -O2 -Iinclude src/*.c test/main.c -o qingluan_test -lbcrypt

Run:
  ./qingluan_test          # self-test + keygen/sign/verify round-trip + tamper
  ./qingluan_kat           # internal determinism KAT (KAT_SIG_QingLuan-<LEVEL>.txt)


Build and Run (official KATs via api_pkc)
-----------------------------------------

Each instance's api_pkc/ folder builds the API_PKC framework + adapter against
THAT instance's ../src and ../include (no LEVEL flag, no cross-folder paths):

  cd Reference_Implementation/QingLuan-128/api_pkc
  make run                 # generate -> output/KAT_SIG_QingLuan-128.txt
  make verify              # validate the published root vectors via the reference
                           # verifier (verify-only); prints "10/10 ... verify OK"

These are the OFFICIAL KAT vectors (NIST/API_PKC framework format:
Count/Seed/PK/SK/M/Sn). The adapter uses the SAME multi-pipe SM3 / SM3-counter
XOF as the Reference (hash_adapter.c is byte-identical to ../src/hash.c), so the
vectors reproduce the reference algorithm exactly. The canonical copies are kept
at the submission root:
  ../../../../Test_Vectors/KAT_SIG_QingLuan-{128,256,384,512}.txt


Parameter Estimation
--------------------

  python ../Supporting_Documentation/rsdp_estimator.py    # self-check vs CROSS Table 5/7

Reproduces the forgery (Prop 6 / Prop 7) and key-recovery cost models behind
Supporting_Documentation/parameters.md. The 384/512 codes are linear
extrapolations and must be re-checked with the official CROSS estimator before
standardization.


Notes
-----

- The four instances share identical source except include/params.h, which is
  fixed to each level (so no -D flag is needed for the reference build). The
  api_pkc/ build passes -DQINGLUAN_<LEVEL> only so the framework driver names
  its output file; the algorithm itself is unaffected.
- Built binaries, *.o, and api_pkc/output/ can be deleted safely; they are
  regenerated on the next build/run and are git-ignored.
